+### Compound Format
+
+Pass `compound: true` to combine units, largest first, with no separators. Zero-valued parts are skipped and leftover milliseconds are dropped (the smallest unit is seconds).
+
+The output is compatible with Go's [`time.ParseDuration`](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration): there are no spaces and hours are the largest unit, so durations of a day or more are expressed in hours.
+
+```ts
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })       // "1h30m"
+ms(3601000, { compound: true })       // "1h1s"
+ms(25 * 3600000 + 30 * 60000, { compound: true }) // "25h30m"
+ms(-5400000, { compound: true })      // "-1h30m"
+ms(500, { compound: true })           // "0s"
+```
+
+`compound` only applies to the short format and is ignored when `long` is set.
+
